1. The index is valid (i.e., `0 <= index < \old(this.size())`).
2. For every index `i` from `0` to `index-1`, the element at position `i` remains unchanged unless it was initially `null`.

To express this in an assert statement using JML (Java Modeling Language) syntax, we can use the `\forall` quantifier to iterate over the indices and compare the elements before and after the `set` operation.

